NAME: Newsletter
OWNER: Content Studio
ACCOUNT: business
WHEN: Every Thursday at 6:43 AM (Australia/Brisbane)
MILESTONE: M3
STATUS: Created paused. Turned on only after Tommy says yes.
---
Switch check: read /workspace/tmec-team/context/routines-on.md. If "Newsletter" isn't listed there as "on" or "test", append "<time> · Newsletter · SKIPPED_OFF" to /workspace/tmec-team/log/runs-<YYYY-MM>.md and stop.
Test mode: if it's listed as "test", send every message to Tommy only, never to a channel or anyone else, and start each message with "TEST". Write state only under /workspace/tmec-team/state/test/, never the live sent keys, alert flags or data files.
Stop check: if /workspace/tmec-team/state/EXTERNAL_WRITES_STOPPED exists, append "<time> · Newsletter · SKIPPED_STOPPED" to the run log and stop, sending nothing. Whoever stopped the team already told Tommy.
Isolation guard: work only in /workspace/tmec-team/ and this account's connected apps. If /workspace/tmec-team/context/owner.md is missing, append "<time> · Newsletter · NO_CLIENT_SOURCE" to the run log and stop. Never use another bot's files, logins or memory.
Lean run: read only what this job needs. Stop with NO_CHANGE only where the job below says nothing changed: append "<time> · Newsletter · NO_CHANGE" to the run log and stop. A report that always goes out never stops here.
Run log: when you finish, append "<time> · Newsletter · EXECUTED · <one-line result>" to /workspace/tmec-team/log/runs-<YYYY-MM>.md, or FAILED with the reason. A source you couldn't read is UNKNOWN in your output, never zero.

First, read your decisions: for each file in /workspace/tmec-team/approved/decisions/ for one of your newsletter items (BOT: content-studio, id starting news-) that isn't in /workspace/tmec-team/state/sent-keys-content-studio.md yet, act on it with the newsletter-issue skill (yes with a matching HASH: create the NEWS- list and email in HubSpot and send or schedule it once, as approved; no: mark it declined; change: redraft as a new item). In test mode, never create or send anything in HubSpot: write what you would have done to /workspace/tmec-team/state/test/.
Then read any new job in /workspace/tmec-team/requests/to-content-studio/ and do it first.
Then use the newsletter-issue skill: gather this week's real items, check the rebate facts against /workspace/tmec-team/data/forecast/rebates.md, build the audience from HubSpot (read-only) with the consent and suppression gates, write the issue, and put it in /workspace/tmec-team/approved/pending/content-studio/ as one item. Fewer than two real items, or a missing or stale source: write NO_CHANGE with the reason and stop. Never send or create anything in HubSpot in this step.
Write /workspace/tmec-team/daily/<today>/content-studio.md: last issue's HubSpot numbers (labelled as HubSpot's), opt-outs seen, the new issue waiting (audience count and held counts, no addresses), anything blocked and why.
